# Lines NoWayOS's tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial
# lines: the kitchen sink's ten screens toured by keys typed on the
# terminal - kitchen-sink.qmp, typed into QEMU's serial port, or through the
# Pi 5's Debug Probe - each screen named as the UI shows it, and each action
# its buttons take. Never what was typed.
SHOWCASE: ui: starting
SHOWCASE: ui: the display is 1920x1064 Rgb565 at scale 2
SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome
SHOWCASE: ui: action Start
SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-text
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-choice
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-checkbox
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing step-notice
SHOWCASE: ui: action Next
SHOWCASE: ui: showing review
SHOWCASE: ui: action Send
SHOWCASE: ui: showing submitting
SHOWCASE: ui: showing failed
SHOWCASE: ui: action Try again
SHOWCASE: ui: showing submitted
SHOWCASE: ui: action Done
SHOWCASE: ui: showing idle-warning
SHOWCASE: ui: action Yes, I am here
SHOWCASE: ui: showing welcome

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic, a
# PD giving up, a record refused or rejected, input dropped anywhere - by the
# UART input PD, at the broker's rate or for want of room in the UI's ring.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!refused
!rejected
!dropped so far
!over its rate
!the UI's ring is full

# Nothing derived from what was typed: no frame's or scan-out hash,
# which the display PD prints only when it is not quiet, and nothing the
# script types - every name starts zqvj, the reference is 9081726354.
# tools/check-quiet requires the hash line, and each text typed to start
# with a text forbidden here.
!display-stub: frame
!zqvj
!9081726354
